('69252d89-046e-5757-8be9-c69fcc6134da','56ac7faf-b261-5a7c-ac6d-8ec5fe5eddf8',4,'picture','تصویر','spoken & written','a thin board with a picture painted on it',null,null,'یک تخته نازک که یک تصویر روی آن نقاشی شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('abe7ff00-9684-550d-a9e7-52d8c24204c3','c36d0de7-d9f1-505b-9be7-d765847d08c7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a sudden strong feeling of fear or nervousness that makes you unable to think clearly or behave sensibly','[ countable usually singular, uncountable ]',null,'ترس و لرز، هراس؛ آشوب (ملّی)؛ هراس (شخصی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['there was (a) panic When the shooting started, there was panic.','cause panic The earthquake caused widespread panic.','feel panic He felt a mild panic.','get into a panic There’s no need to get into a panic.','throw/send somebody into a panic The innocent question threw her into a panic.','panic breaks out (= starts among a group of people ) Suddenly, everything went dark and panic broke out.','panic sets in (= starts ) Before panic could set in, she realised that the clock was fast.','panic ensues formal (= happens after something else happens ) Panic ensued as people ran out of the burning building.','panic rises within somebody (= someone starts to feel panic ) She felt panic rising within her.','panic spreads (= starts to affect more people in more places ) Panic spread as news of the invasion reached Paris.','a big/huge panic There was a big panic about the virus last year.','growing/mounting/rising panic (= increasing panic ) She quickly packed a bag, trying all the time to control her mounting panic.','total/sheer panic A wave of total panic swept across her.','blind panic (= a very strong feeling of fear ) He ran to the library in blind panic.','sudden panic Florrie exclaimed in sudden panic: ‘I’ve left my bag on the bus!’','mild panic (= a slight feeling of panic ) There was a note of mild panic in her voice.','momentary panic (= panic that does not last long ) Her momentary panic faded.','a state of panic She was in a constant state of panic that he would carry out his threat.','a sense/feeling of panic She looked out to sea with a rising sense of panic.','a wave/surge of panic (= a feeling of panic that you suddenly have ) A sudden wave of panic overcame him.','a panic attack He had had a panic attack in the street.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The children fled in panic.","translation":"بچه ها وحشت زده فرار کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722222.mp3"},{"sentence":"a feeling of sheer panic (= complete panic )","translation":"احساس وحشت محض (= وحشت کامل)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722223.mp3"},{"sentence":"She got into a panic when she couldn’t find the tickets.","translation":"وقتی بلیط ها را پیدا نکرد، دچار وحشت شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722227.mp3"},{"sentence":"The whole nation is in a state of panic following the attacks.","translation":"همه ملت در پی این حملات در وحشت هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722231.mp3"},{"sentence":"She suffers from terrible panic attacks .","translation":"او از حملات وحشتناک وحشتناک رنج می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001722235.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('334aa213-6ed6-5489-aa37-97d5b5345493','c36d0de7-d9f1-505b-9be7-d765847d08c7',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which people are suddenly made very anxious , and make quick decisions without thinking carefully','[ countable usually singular, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن افراد به طور ناگهانی بسیار مضطرب می شوند و بدون تفکر دقیق تصمیمات سریع می گیرند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['there was (a) panic When the shooting started, there was panic.','cause panic The earthquake caused widespread panic.','feel panic He felt a mild panic.','get into a panic There’s no need to get into a panic.','throw/send somebody into a panic The innocent question threw her into a panic.','panic breaks out (= starts among a group of people ) Suddenly, everything went dark and panic broke out.','panic sets in (= starts ) Before panic could set in, she realised that the clock was fast.','panic ensues formal (= happens after something else happens ) Panic ensued as people ran out of the burning building.','panic rises within somebody (= someone starts to feel panic ) She felt panic rising within her.','panic spreads (= starts to affect more people in more places ) Panic spread as news of the invasion reached Paris.','a big/huge panic There was a big panic about the virus last year.','growing/mounting/rising panic (= increasing panic ) She quickly packed a bag, trying all the time to control her mounting panic.','total/sheer panic A wave of total panic swept across her.','blind panic (= a very strong feeling of fear ) He ran to the library in blind panic.','sudden panic Florrie exclaimed in sudden panic: ‘I’ve left my bag on the bus!’','mild panic (= a slight feeling of panic ) There was a note of mild panic in her voice.','momentary panic (= panic that does not last long ) Her momentary panic faded.','a state of panic She was in a constant state of panic that he would carry out his threat.','a sense/feeling of panic She looked out to sea with a rising sense of panic.','a wave/surge of panic (= a feeling of panic that you suddenly have ) A sudden wave of panic overcame him.','a panic attack He had had a panic attack in the street.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the recent panic over the safety of baby milk","translation":"وحشت اخیر در مورد ایمنی شیر کودک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000362590.mp3"},{"sentence":"a wave of panic selling in Hong Kong","translation":"موجی از فروش وحشت در هنگ کنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000362593.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
