('72f0ea10-5e00-5176-8525-723b5aea6d39','7ea7a4e8-2134-50f4-a96a-f97ba3e53795',1,null,null,'spoken & written','Her Majesty the Queen - the official title of the queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland. The Queen is the official head of state of Britain and of other countries in the Commonwealth , but has little real political power. She has to give her official agreement ( Royal Assent ) to all new laws before they can actually become laws but in fact she does not have the right to refuse this agreement.',null,'see also Elizabeth II, Queen','اعلیحضرت ملکه - عنوان رسمی ملکه پادشاهی متحد بریتانیای کبیر و ایرلند شمالی. ملکه رئیس رسمی دولت بریتانیا و سایر کشورهای مشترک المنافع است، اما قدرت سیاسی واقعی کمی دارد. او باید موافقت رسمی خود (موافقت سلطنتی) را برای همه قوانین جدید قبل از اینکه واقعاً به قانون تبدیل شوند، بدهد، اما در واقع حق ندارد از این توافقنامه امتناع کند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('108890ed-8a77-5f44-a2d5-ec83350ae808','c405662a-f3c5-5e41-8e58-ac8818b47cc1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a British rock group who were very popular in the 1970s and 1980s, and whose songs include Bohemian Rhapsody and We Are the Champions . Their main singer was Freddie Mercury , and they were known especially for playing to very large crowds , for example in football stadium s .',null,null,'یک گروه راک بریتانیایی که در دهه‌های 1970 و 1980 بسیار محبوب بودند و آهنگ‌هایش شامل Bohemian Rhapsody و We Are the Champions است. خواننده اصلی آنها فردی مرکوری بود و آنها به ویژه به خاطر بازی در میان جمعیت بسیار زیاد، به عنوان مثال در استادیوم های فوتبال، شناخته شده بودند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('54e29b4a-6fa7-59d0-aa71-fb4c65bdcafc','43a7ac3d-266c-5f1c-9381-87e51593c353',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a line of people waiting to enter a building , buy something etc, or a line of vehicles waiting to move',null,null,'صف، نوبت (منتظران)؛ صف (کار)؛ صف (شلوار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stand/wait in a queue She stood in the queue at the checkout.','be in a queue I''ve been in this queue for fifteen minutes.','form a queue Other passengers for the train were forming a queue.','join a queue He went back inside to join the queue for the toilets.','take your place in a queue (= join it ) I walked to the bus stop and took my place in the queue.','jump the queue (= go to the front rather than joining the end of a queue ) An argument developed when she tried to jump the queue.','a queue forms A queue had formed outside the shop.','a queue stretches somewhere The queue stretched the full length of the building.','long/big Already a long queue had formed outside the concert hall There was a big queue.','small There was a small queue of people waiting to see the doctor.','an orderly queue (= with no bad behaviour or pushing in front of other people ) She told the children to form an orderly queue.','the front/head of the queue He pushed his way to the front of the queue.','the back/end of the queue Get to the back of the queue!','be first in a queue I wanted to be first in the queue when the doors opened.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We stood in a queue for half an hour.","translation":"نیم ساعت در صف ایستادیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000467606.mp3"},{"sentence":"You’ll have to join the queue .","translation":"شما باید به صف بپیوندید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583187.mp3"},{"sentence":"a queue of people waiting for the bus","translation":"صفی از مردم در انتظار اتوبوس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583183.mp3"},{"sentence":"the queue for the toilets","translation":"صف توالت ها","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583186.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a long queue to get into the cinema.","translation":"یک صف طولانی برای ورود به سینما وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769840.mp3"},{"sentence":"At last we got to the front of the queue.","translation":"بالاخره به جلوی صف رسیدیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769841.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('ca047474-6ac7-58ae-ae0f-51f609cda757','43a7ac3d-266c-5f1c-9381-87e51593c353',2,null,null,'spoken & written','all the people who are waiting to have or get something',null,null,'همه افرادی که منتظرند چیزی داشته باشند یا به دست بیاورند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stand/wait in a queue She stood in the queue at the checkout.','be in a queue I''ve been in this queue for fifteen minutes.','form a queue Other passengers for the train were forming a queue.','join a queue He went back inside to join the queue for the toilets.','take your place in a queue (= join it ) I walked to the bus stop and took my place in the queue.','jump the queue (= go to the front rather than joining the end of a queue ) An argument developed when she tried to jump the queue.','a queue forms A queue had formed outside the shop.','a queue stretches somewhere The queue stretched the full length of the building.','long/big Already a long queue had formed outside the concert hall There was a big queue.','small There was a small queue of people waiting to see the doctor.','an orderly queue (= with no bad behaviour or pushing in front of other people ) She told the children to form an orderly queue.','the front/head of the queue He pushed his way to the front of the queue.','the back/end of the queue Get to the back of the queue!','be first in a queue I wanted to be first in the queue when the doors opened.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’ll have to join the housing queue.","translation":"شما باید به صف مسکن بپیوندید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583195.mp3"},{"sentence":"the queue for kidney transplant operations","translation":"صف عمل پیوند کلیه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583198.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is possible to jump the queue (= get something before people who have been waiting longer ) if you are prepared to pay for your treatment.","translation":"اگر آماده باشید هزینه درمان خود را بپردازید، ممکن است از صف بپرید (= چیزی را قبل از افرادی که مدت بیشتری منتظر بوده اند دریافت کنید).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769844.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
