('2bc9373f-513c-5b5b-820a-1b87e51f5f59','049bf4a9-e836-5b76-9501-2aa0ad3e94a1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling about something','[ countable ]',null,'حس، احساس؛ عقل (مشترک)؛ منظر (حس)؛ معنا (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a strong/great sense of something He had a strong sense of responsibility.','a real sense of something (= a strong feeling ) Children need to feel a real sense of belonging.','a deep sense of something (= a very strong feeling ) He felt a deep sense of disappointment.','a growing sense of something (= becoming stronger ) She looked around with a growing sense of unease.','a vague/slight sense of something (= not very strong ) There was a slight sense of embarrassment.','feel/have a sense of something I felt a great sense of pride.','give somebody a sense of something The job gave her a sense of control over her life.','convey a sense of something We want to convey our sense of excitement to the audience.','a sense of relief/panic/guilt etc We reached the medical centre with a sense of relief.','a sense of purpose/direction (= a feeling that you know what you are trying to achieve ) Becoming a mother had given her a new sense of purpose.','a sense of urgency (= a feeling that something is urgent ) The rescuers felt a real sense of urgency now.','a sense of responsibility/duty (= a feeling that you must do something because it is right ) Parents try to give their children a sense of responsibility.','a sense of loss (= a feeling of sadness for someone or something you no longer have ) Many women experience a sense of loss when their children leave home.','a sense of achievement/satisfaction (= a feeling that you have achieved something good ) Even a small success gives a sense of achievement.','a sense of security (= a feeling that you are safe ) A lack of trust in the parents can undermine the child''s sense of security at home.','a false sense of security (= a feeling that you are safe, which is not actually true ) They were lulled into a false sense of security.','a sense of identity (= a feeling of knowing who you are and how you belong to a community ) Change can threaten our fragile sense of identity.','a sense of belonging (= a feeling that you belong to a group ) The organization tries to foster a sense of belonging through these social events.','a sense of occasion (= a feeling that an event is special or important ) It was a marvellous day and there was a real sense of occasion.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Afterwards, I felt a great sense of relief.","translation":"بعد از آن، احساس آرامش زیادی کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794070.mp3"},{"sentence":"A sense of panic has spread over the country.","translation":"احساس وحشت سراسر کشور را فرا گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001825637.mp3"},{"sentence":"Employees need the sense of being appreciated.","translation":"کارمندان به احساس قدردانی نیاز دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794085.mp3"},{"sentence":"He looked around the room with a sense of achievement.","translation":"با حس موفقیت به اطراف اتاق نگاه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794082.mp3"},{"sentence":"I had the sense that he was lying.","translation":"حس میکردم داره دروغ میگه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000700676.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('5fcb9fee-ab2a-5fbf-a886-1cb6c9807964','049bf4a9-e836-5b76-9501-2aa0ad3e94a1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the ability to understand or judge something','[ singular ]',null,'توانایی درک یا قضاوت در مورد چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I like Pam – she has a really good sense of humour .","translation":"من پم را دوست دارم - او حس شوخ طبعی خوبی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794105.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was dark and he had completely lost his sense of direction .","translation":"هوا تاریک بود و حس جهت گیری خود را کاملا از دست داده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794114.mp3"},{"sentence":"Let’s keep a sense of proportion, and not rush to any hasty conclusions.","translation":"بیایید حس نسبت را حفظ کنیم و برای نتیجه گیری عجولانه عجله نکنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001825638.mp3"},{"sentence":"Kids have a natural sense of justice .","translation":"بچه ها حس طبیعی عدالت دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794097.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('d2f8bc89-17b8-5ca9-a064-23cda2475efa','049bf4a9-e836-5b76-9501-2aa0ad3e94a1',3,null,null,'spoken & written','one of the five natural powers of sight , hearing, feeling, taste , and smell , that give us information about the things around us','[ countable ]','sixth sense','یکی از پنج نیروی طبیعی بینایی، شنوایی، احساس، چشایی و بویایی که به ما اطلاعاتی در مورد چیزهای اطرافمان می دهد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has a good sense of smell.","translation":"او حس بویایی خوبی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001825644.mp3"},{"sentence":"Cats have a very acute sense of hearing (= very good, so that they can hear even the smallest sound ) .","translation":"گربه ها حس شنوایی بسیار حاد دارند (= بسیار خوب، به طوری که می توانند حتی کوچکترین صدا را بشنوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000700704.mp3"},{"sentence":"Combinations of flavors, textures, and color that can delight the senses .","translation":"ترکیبی از طعم ها، بافت ها و رنگ ها که می تواند حواس را به وجد بیاورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020221.mp3"},{"sentence":"the five senses (= all of the senses )","translation":"حواس پنج گانه (= همه حواس)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794207.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('1ed5b355-cf0e-54bb-a8a1-e503a1bca112','049bf4a9-e836-5b76-9501-2aa0ad3e94a1',4,null,null,'spoken','when someone makes sensible or practical decisions, or behaves in a sensible practical way','[ uncountable ]','common sense','زمانی که شخصی تصمیمات معقول یا عملی می گیرد یا به شیوه عملی معقولی رفتار می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You should have had the sense to turn off the electricity first.","translation":"شما باید اول عقل را می داشتید که برق را خاموش کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794135.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s no sense in getting upset about it now.","translation":"حالا دیگر ناراحت شدن از این بابت معنایی ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794143.mp3"},{"sentence":"I wish the politicians would see sense and stop the war.","translation":"ای کاش سیاستمداران عقل می دیدند و جنگ را متوقف می کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001794147.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
