('91771bfe-9731-51c8-b3f6-74d1a74c1b1a','5e63aea7-56eb-52bf-97c9-32dca2578ee8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the brightness that something has when light shines on it','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'روشنایی که وقتی نور به چیزی می تابد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Lucy’s dark hair seemed to have lost its shine.","translation":"به نظر می رسید موهای تیره لوسی درخشش خود را از دست داده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588681.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('29f45bdd-2df3-51bd-b2dd-861a49b94afe','5e63aea7-56eb-52bf-97c9-32dca2578ee8',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'take a shine to somebody',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e0d41b0d-56d0-5e77-8b78-142cd90def71','97cef72a-2a93-5322-965e-eec817d0f02d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a piece of clothing that covers the upper part of your body and your arms , usually has a collar , and is fastened at the front by buttons',null,null,'پیراهن، پیراهنی (دوخت)؛ پیراهن (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I have to wear a shirt and tie to work.","translation":"برای سرکار باید پیراهن و کراوات بپوشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000713835.mp3"},{"sentence":"a check shirt","translation":"یک پیراهن چک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588759.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2ef7a2d0-54ec-52f7-b6db-9331fe35acb4','97cef72a-2a93-5322-965e-eec817d0f02d',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'keep your shirt on','پیراهن، پیراهنی (دوخت)؛ پیراهن (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7aa3c74b-4ca0-5746-ba1c-13a4560770be','97cef72a-2a93-5322-965e-eec817d0f02d',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'put/bet/stake your shirt on something','پیراهن، پیراهنی (دوخت)؛ پیراهن (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e903e0d4-ae24-5b8a-8071-0c6029df7d89','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',1,'unexpected event/situation','رویداد/وضعیت غیرمنتظره','spoken & written','if something that happens is a shock, you did not expect it, and it makes you feel very surprised , and usually upset','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'شوک، صدمه؛ برق‌گرفتگی (برق)؛ شوک (بازار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/great shock It was a great shock to find out he had been lying.','a terrible/awful shock Her death was a terrible shock to everyone.','a complete/total shock No one expected the factory to close – it was a complete shock.','a nasty shock especially British English (= one that is very unpleasant and upsetting ) Come and sit down. You’ve had a nasty shock.','a rude shock formal (= one that is unexpected and unpleasant but not serious ) Shopping for food in Miyako brought a rude shock. The prices were breathtaking.','get/have a shock I got a shock when I saw how thin he had become.','give somebody a shock Oh, you gave me quite a shock.','get over/recover from a shock He hasn’t got over the shock of losing his job yet.','die of shock informal (= be very surprised ) I nearly died of shock when I saw Helen at the door.','come as a shock (= be very unexpected ) The collapse of the company came as a shock to us all.','be a bit of a shock British English especially spoken (= be a shock, but not very serious or unpleasant ) I wasn’t expecting to win, so it was a bit of a shock.','be a shock to the system (= be strange because you are not used to something ) Having to work full-time again was quite a shock to the system.','be in for a shock (= be likely to have a shock ) Anyone who thinks that bringing up children is easy is in for a shock.','be in a state of shock ( also be in deep shock ) (= be very shocked and upset ) Eva left the room in a state of shock.','get the shock of your life (= get a very big shock ) He got the shock of his life when he found out who I was.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The news of his death came as a great shock to everyone.","translation":"خبر درگذشت او شوک بزرگی برای همه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001452.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was a real shock to hear that the factory would have to close.","translation":"شنیدن اینکه کارخانه باید تعطیل شود واقعاً شوک بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714256.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c03d92da-54be-54af-8a93-6b148c0db045','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',2,'unexpected unpleasant feeling','احساس ناخوشایند غیر منتظره','spoken & written','the feeling of surprise and disbelief you have when something very unexpected happens, especially something bad or frightening','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'احساس غافلگیری و ناباوری وقتی اتفاقی بسیار غیرمنتظره می افتد، به خصوص اتفاق بد یا ترسناک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/great shock It was a great shock to find out he had been lying.','a terrible/awful shock Her death was a terrible shock to everyone.','a complete/total shock No one expected the factory to close – it was a complete shock.','a nasty shock especially British English (= one that is very unpleasant and upsetting ) Come and sit down. You’ve had a nasty shock.','a rude shock formal (= one that is unexpected and unpleasant but not serious ) Shopping for food in Miyako brought a rude shock. The prices were breathtaking.','get/have a shock I got a shock when I saw how thin he had become.','give somebody a shock Oh, you gave me quite a shock.','get over/recover from a shock He hasn’t got over the shock of losing his job yet.','die of shock informal (= be very surprised ) I nearly died of shock when I saw Helen at the door.','come as a shock (= be very unexpected ) The collapse of the company came as a shock to us all.','be a bit of a shock British English especially spoken (= be a shock, but not very serious or unpleasant ) I wasn’t expecting to win, so it was a bit of a shock.','be a shock to the system (= be strange because you are not used to something ) Having to work full-time again was quite a shock to the system.','be in for a shock (= be likely to have a shock ) Anyone who thinks that bringing up children is easy is in for a shock.','be in a state of shock ( also be in deep shock ) (= be very shocked and upset ) Eva left the room in a state of shock.','get the shock of your life (= get a very big shock ) He got the shock of his life when he found out who I was.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was shaking with shock and humiliation.","translation":"از شوک و تحقیر می لرزید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588901.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mom’s never really gotten over the shock of Dad’s death.","translation":"مادر واقعاً هرگز از شوک مرگ پدر غلبه نکرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588908.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e1640d72-b17e-573c-9449-9ba61c9a2dde','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',3,'medical','پزشکی','spoken & written','a medical condition in which someone looks pale and their heart and lungs are not working correctly, usually after a sudden very unpleasant experience','[ uncountable ]',null,'یک وضعیت پزشکی که در آن شخصی رنگ پریده به نظر می رسد و قلب و ریه های او به درستی کار نمی کنند، معمولاً پس از یک تجربه ناگهانی بسیار ناخوشایند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was bleeding from the head and suffering from shock .","translation":"از سرش خون می آمد و از شوک رنج می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588919.mp3"},{"sentence":"He is clearly in a state of shock .","translation":"او به وضوح در حالت شوک است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714284.mp3"},{"sentence":"The tanker driver was treated for shock and released.","translation":"راننده تانکر تحت درمان شوک قرار گرفت و مرخص شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588923.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('32507d5d-803a-594a-9002-8d97bbf0b055','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',4,'electricity','برق','spoken & written','an electric shock','[ countable ]',null,'یک شوک الکتریکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('cc967f4d-cd66-56a4-abab-d7af29351dba','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',5,'vehicle','وسیله نقلیه','spoken & written','a shock absorber','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'یک ضربه گیر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d4ec3e4b-940c-5779-b95f-6d3cc530aa34','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'shock of hair','شوک، صدمه؛ برق‌گرفتگی (برق)؛ شوک (بازار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f4ab2dd3-383c-5e9e-92e3-0f0afe8b0c46','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',7,'sudden change','تغییر ناگهانی','spoken & written','a sudden unexpected change which threatens the economic situation, way of life, or traditions of a group of people – used especially in news reports','[ countable ]',null,'تغییر ناگهانی غیرمنتظره ای که وضعیت اقتصادی، شیوه زندگی یا سنت های گروهی از مردم را تهدید می کند - به ویژه در گزارش های خبری استفاده می شود.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the oil shocks of the 1970s","translation":"شوک های نفتی دهه 1970","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588947.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('361791ba-45b2-56d2-93e3-4168cca2d756','04c65505-7e89-5b68-bb8d-6eba7e7900a4',8,'shaking','تکان دادن','spoken & written','violent shaking caused for example by an explosion or earthquake','[ countable, uncountable ]','shock wave , culture shock , shocked , shell shock , toxic shock syndrome','لرزش شدید ناشی از انفجار یا زلزله','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The shock was felt miles away.","translation":"شوک کیلومترها دورتر احساس شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714305.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('054237a5-886e-573d-b466-d9c520cf7b04','11008fbf-c7ca-5576-aab9-15af37671536',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone feel very surprised and upset, and unable to believe what has happened','[ transitive ]',null,'وادار کردن کسی احساس شگفتی و ناراحتی کند و نتواند آنچه اتفاق افتاده را باور کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The hatred in her voice shocked him.","translation":"نفرت در صدای او او را شوکه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714363.mp3"},{"sentence":"They had been shocked to hear that the hospital was closing down.","translation":"آنها از شنیدن این که بیمارستان در حال تعطیل شدن است، شوکه شده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588960.mp3"},{"sentence":"It shocked me to think how close we had come to being killed.","translation":"فکر اینکه چقدر به کشته شدن نزدیک شده بودیم، شوکه شدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001774955.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was shocked into action by the desperate situation in the orphanages.","translation":"او از وضعیت ناامیدکننده یتیم خانه ها شوکه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588963.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('6c7f31b9-14a6-5db3-974a-d439a06399a1','11008fbf-c7ca-5576-aab9-15af37671536',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone feel very offended , by talking or behaving in an immoral or socially unacceptable way','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'با صحبت کردن یا رفتار غیراخلاقی یا غیرقابل قبول از نظر اجتماعی به شخصی احساس آزار رساندن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He seems to enjoy shocking people.","translation":"به نظر می رسد او از شوکه کردن مردم لذت می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714371.mp3"},{"sentence":"Just ignore the bad language – they only do it to shock.","translation":"فقط زبان بد را نادیده بگیرید - آنها این کار را فقط برای شوکه کردن انجام می دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714372.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
