most waking up ) I lay in the garden, drifting in and out of sleep.','cry yourself to sleep (= cry until you fall asleep ) I used to cry myself to sleep every night.','fall into a deep/long etc sleep (= start sleeping deeply, for a long time etc ) He lay down on his bed and fell into a deep sleep.','wake/be woken from a deep/long etc sleep A very long time later I woke from a deep sleep.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I had a little sleep in the afternoon.","translation":"بعد از ظهر کمی خوابیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001479.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was woken from a deep sleep by a ring at the door.","translation":"او را از خواب عمیق با حلقه ای که در در بود بیدار کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000664912.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
