('6fe4f2a0-830d-5b8a-bebf-429aa77fa567','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',1,'intelligent','باهوش','spoken & written','intelligent or sensible',null,null,'باهوش، زیرک؛ شیک (پوشاک)؛ خوش‌سلیقه (فرد)',array['clever']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The smart kids get good grades and go off to college.","translation":"بچه های باهوش نمرات خوبی می گیرند و به دانشگاه می روند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668377.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was smart enough to wait for a week.","translation":"آنقدر باهوش بودم که یک هفته صبر کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585653.mp3"},{"sentence":"His decision to become a director was a smart move (= sensible thing to do ) .","translation":"تصمیم او برای کارگردان شدن یک حرکت هوشمندانه (= کار معقولانه) بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585654.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('5d654c25-5239-5891-8af2-e3a669998520','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',2,'disrespectful','بی احترامی','spoken & written','trying to seem clever in a disrespectful way',null,null,'سعی می کند به روشی غیر محترمانه باهوش به نظر برسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Don’t get smart with me, young man.","translation":"با من زرنگ نشو، مرد جوان.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789208.mp3"},{"sentence":"He made some smart remark.","translation":"او اظهار نظر هوشمندانه ای کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789212.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('219633f1-2e2e-52f4-9f58-216b84641233','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',3,'neat','مرتب','spoken & written','a smart person is wearing neat attractive clothes and has a generally tidy appearance',null,null,'یک فرد باهوش لباس های جذاب و مرتبی می پوشد و ظاهری مرتب دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’re looking very smart .","translation":"خیلی باهوش به نظر میای","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668388.mp3"},{"sentence":"a smart black suit","translation":"یک کت و شلوار مشکی هوشمند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585676.mp3"},{"sentence":"smart new offices","translation":"دفاتر هوشمند جدید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585677.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('0ddb599c-c420-5df6-aeed-b3a8cf9d34e9','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',4,'fashionable','مد روز','spoken & written','fashionable or used by fashionable people',null,null,'مد روز یا مورد استفاده افراد شیک پوش','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"one of Bonn’s smartest restaurants","translation":"یکی از باهوش ترین رستوران های بن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668394.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1a51b356-11ad-5990-b2a0-6585fe260dda','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',5,'technology','تکنولوژی','spoken & written','smart machines , weapons , materials etc are controlled by computers and are designed to react in a suitable way depending on the situation',null,null,'ماشین‌های هوشمند، سلاح‌ها، مواد و غیره توسط رایانه کنترل می‌شوند و به گونه‌ای طراحی شده‌اند که بسته به موقعیت، واکنش مناسب نشان دهند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"smart weapons","translation":"سلاح های هوشمند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789216.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('472f5485-05a3-5345-95d8-65c938b7e8d5','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the smart money is on somebody/something','باهوش، زیرک؛ شیک (پوشاک)؛ خوش‌سلیقه (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('72b9e7fa-82d5-5390-b11d-c0a6b4f3350d','3ea26e8d-3cf5-51de-938c-90b6915a766c',7,'quick','سریع','spoken & written','a smart movement is done quickly, especially with force',null,null,'یک حرکت هوشمند به سرعت انجام می شود، به خصوص با زور','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a smart blow on the head","translation":"ضربه هوشمندانه به سر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668399.mp3"},{"sentence":"She set off at a smart pace (= fairly fast ) .","translation":"او با سرعتی هوشمندانه به راه افتاد (= نسبتاً سریع).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585687.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('be77c954-5d2c-58e0-8825-882654d13ce3','c3d604f8-1f64-5819-8761-f60ec7b2e2d9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to be upset because someone has hurt your feelings or offended you',null,null,'از اینکه کسی احساسات شما را جریحه دار کرده یا به شما توهین کرده است ناراحت باشید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was still smarting from the insult.","translation":"از توهین هنوز هوشیار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668430.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('46724494-2b8d-5287-a456-232c691e8027','c3d604f8-1f64-5819-8761-f60ec7b2e2d9',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a part of your body smarts, it hurts with a stinging pain',null,null,'اگر قسمتی از بدن شما هوشمند باشد، با درد گزنده درد می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"My eyes were smarting with the smoke.","translation":"چشمانم از دود هوشمند شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668435.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5a7e2fc8-2684-55e2-8ca3-b323435e4242','3176540c-c15d-5cfb-be86-a5680c977417',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the quality that people and animals recognize by using their nose','[ countable ]',null,'بوی، بو؛ بو (خوب)؛ بو (طبیعت)؛ بوی (شخص)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong There was a strong smell of burning in the air.','faint (= not strong ) I noticed a faint smell of perfume.','overpowering (= very strong ) The smell of disinfectant was overpowering.','nice/pleasant/lovely There was a lovely smell of fresh coffee.','bad/unpleasant/horrible etc The smell in the shed was awful.','a strange/funny/odd smell What’s that funny smell?','a sweet smell She liked the sweet smell of hay in the barn.','a delicious smell (= a pleasant smell of food ) There were delicious smells emanating from the kitchen.','a sickly smell (= sweet and unpleasant ) the sweet, sickly smell of decaying human flesh','a pungent smell formal (= strong and unpleasant ) A pungent smell of garlic filled the air.','an acrid smell (= strong and bitter ) The acrid smell of smoke clung about the place.','a musty/stale/sour smell (= old and not fresh ) The clothes in the wardrobe had a damp musty smell.','have a strong/sweet etc smell The flowers had a lovely sweet smell.','be filled with a smell The house was filled with the smell of baking bread.','give off a smell (= produce a smell ) Rubber gives off a strong smell when it is burned.','notice/smell a smell ( also detect a smell formal ) He detected a faint smell of blood.','a smell comes from somewhere ( also a smell emanates from somewhere formal ) A delicious smell of baking came from the kitchen. He was getting complaints about the smell emanating from his shop.','a smell wafts somewhere (= moves there through the air ) The smells wafting up the stairs from the kitchen were making her feel hungry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The air was filled with the smell of flowers.","translation":"هوا پر شده بود از بوی گل.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668841.mp3"},{"sentence":"What’s that horrible smell?","translation":"آن بوی وحشتناک چیست؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001484.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c27e1238-b9b7-589f-8eb5-77b0ab78110a','3176540c-c15d-5cfb-be86-a5680c977417',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an unpleasant smell','[ countable ]',null,'بوی نامطبوع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong There was a strong smell of burning in the air.','faint (= not strong ) I noticed a faint smell of perfume.','overpowering (= very strong ) The smell of disinfectant was overpowering.','nice/pleasant/lovely There was a lovely smell of fresh coffee.','bad/unpleasant/horrible etc The smell in the shed was awful.','a strange/funny/odd smell What’s that funny smell?','a sweet smell She liked the sweet smell of hay in the barn.','a delicious smell (= a pleasant smell of food ) There were delicious smells emanating from the kitchen.','a sickly smell (= sweet and unpleasant ) the sweet, sickly smell of decaying human flesh','a pungent smell formal (= strong and unpleasant ) A pungent smell of garlic filled the air.','an acrid smell (= strong and bitter ) The acrid smell of smoke clung about the place.','a musty/stale/sour smell (= old and not fresh ) The clothes in the wardrobe had a damp musty smell.','have a strong/sweet etc smell The flowers had a lovely sweet smell.','be filled with a smell The house was filled with the smell of baking bread.','give off a smell (= produce a smell ) Rubber gives off a strong smell when it is burned.','notice/smell a smell ( also detect a smell formal ) He detected a faint smell of blood.','a smell comes from somewhere ( also a smell emanates from somewhere formal ) A delicious smell of baking came from the kitchen. He was getting complaints about the smell emanating from his shop.','a smell wafts somewhere (= moves there through the air ) The smells wafting up the stairs from the kitchen were making her feel hungry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I think the smell’s getting worse.","translation":"فکر می کنم بوی بدتر می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668852.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3dd7feb5-d6b4-5413-8e6e-f404fed9c4b8','3176540c-c15d-5cfb-be86-a5680c977417',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the ability to notice or recognize smells','[ uncountable ]',null,'توانایی تشخیص یا تشخیص بوها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong There was a strong smell of burning in the air.','faint (= not strong ) I noticed a faint smell of perfume.','overpowering (= very strong ) The smell of disinfectant was overpowering.','nice/pleasant/lovely There was a lovely smell of fresh coffee.','bad/unpleasant/horrible etc The smell in the shed was awful.','a strange/funny/odd smell What’s that funny smell?','a sweet smell She liked the sweet smell of hay in the barn.','a delicious smell (= a pleasant smell of food ) There were delicious smells emanating from the kitchen.','a sickly smell (= sweet and unpleasant ) the sweet, sickly smell of decaying human flesh','a pungent smell formal (= strong and unpleasant ) A pungent smell of garlic filled the air.','an acrid smell (= strong and bitter ) The acrid smell of smoke clung about the place.','a musty/stale/sour smell (= old and not fresh ) The clothes in the wardrobe had a damp musty smell.','have a strong/sweet etc smell The flowers had a lovely sweet smell.','be filled with a smell The house was filled with the smell of baking bread.','give off a smell (= produce a smell ) Rubber gives off a strong smell when it is burned.','notice/smell a smell ( also detect a smell formal ) He detected a faint smell of blood.','a smell comes from somewhere ( also a smell emanates from somewhere formal ) A delicious smell of baking came from the kitchen. He was getting complaints about the smell emanating from his shop.','a smell wafts somewhere (= moves there through the air ) The smells wafting up the stairs from the kitchen were making her feel hungry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"loss of taste and smell","translation":"از دست دادن چشایی و بویایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585760.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dogs have a very good sense of smell .","translation":"سگ ها حس بویایی بسیار خوبی دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668868.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('7bb81127-ef6a-5c80-94b1-2d03ebdd4957','3176540c-c15d-5cfb-be86-a5680c977417',4,null,null,'spoken & written','an act of smelling something','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'عمل بوییدن چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong There was a strong smell of burning in the air.','faint (= not strong ) I noticed a faint smell of perfume.','overpowering (= very strong ) The smell of disinfectant was overpowering.','nice/pleasant/lovely There was a lovely smell of fresh coffee.','bad/unpleasant/horrible etc The smell in the shed was awful.','a strange/funny/odd smell What’s that funny smell?','a sweet smell She liked the sweet smell of hay in the barn.','a delicious smell (= a pleasant smell of food ) There were delicious smells emanating from the kitchen.','a sickly smell (= sweet and unpleasant ) the sweet, sickly smell of decaying human flesh','a pungent smell formal (= strong and unpleasant ) A pungent smell of garlic filled the air.','an acrid smell (= strong and bitter ) The acrid smell of smoke clung about the place.','a musty/stale/sour smell (= old and not fresh ) The clothes in the wardrobe had a damp musty smell.','have a strong/sweet etc smell The flowers had a lovely sweet smell.','be filled with a smell The house was filled with the smell of baking bread.','give off a smell (= produce a smell ) Rubber gives off a strong smell when it is burned.','notice/smell a smell ( also detect a smell formal ) He detected a faint smell of blood.','a smell comes from somewhere ( also a smell emanates from somewhere formal ) A delicious smell of baking came from the kitchen. He was getting complaints about the smell emanating from his shop.','a smell wafts somewhere (= moves there through the air ) The smells wafting up the stairs from the kitchen were making her feel hungry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Have a smell of this cheese; does it seem all right?","translation":"بوی این پنیر را داشته باشید؛ به نظر می رسد خوب است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789229.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('73e5ecc1-026e-5f7b-ab85-3e0d7a0a4c24','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',1,'notice a smell','متوجه بو','spoken & written','to notice or recognize a particular smell','[ transitive ]',null,'بو دادن؛ استشمام کردن (بوی)؛ بو دادن (خوراک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I can smell burning.","translation":"بوی سوختگی را حس می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668916.mp3"},{"sentence":"Can you smell something?","translation":"آیا می توانید چیزی را بو کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585768.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9a817e4a-df02-5896-865c-b10e6042ba58','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',2,'have a smell','بو داشتن','spoken & written','to have a particular smell','[ linking verb ]',null,'برای داشتن بوی خاصی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['smell good/nice etc The food smelled good.','smell delicious That soup smells delicious.','smell fresh Rub your chopping board with lemon to keep it smelling fresh.','smell sweet A ripe melon will smell sweet.','smell bad/awful etc Cigarettes make your clothes smell awful.','smell funny/strange This place smells funny sometimes.','smell strongly of something The man smelled strongly of alcohol.','smell faintly of something His suit smelled faintly of tobacco.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The stew smelled delicious.","translation":"خورش بوی خوشمزه می داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668896.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mm! Something smells good!","translation":"مم! یه چیزی بوی خوبی میده!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001980707.mp3"},{"sentence":"The water smells funny.","translation":"آب بوی خنده‌داری می‌دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00812.mp3"},{"sentence":"My clothes smelt of smoke.","translation":"لباس هایم بوی دود می داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668900.mp3"},{"sentence":"It smells like rotten eggs.","translation":"بوی تخم مرغ گندیده می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585774.mp3"},{"sentence":"sweet-smelling flowers","translation":"گلهای خوشبو","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000605103.mp3"},{"sentence":"The cream smells funny (= it has a strange smell )","translation":"کرم بوی خنده دار می دهد (= بوی عجیبی دارد)","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,7),
('db146739-1bd5-55dd-8846-ae079dd1c251','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',3,'have a bad smell','بوی بدی دارند','spoken & written','to have an unpleasant smell','[ intransitive ]',null,'برای داشتن بوی نامطبوع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Your feet smell!","translation":"پاهایت بو می دهد!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668909.mp3"},{"sentence":"The room smelled to high heaven (= had a very bad smell ) .","translation":"اتاق بوی بهشت ​​بلند می داد (= بوی بسیار بدی می داد ) .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001980711.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('75912fcc-ce05-5fb7-ba43-ac80e85be007','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',4,'put your nose near something','بینی خود را نزدیک چیزی قرار دهید','spoken & written','to put your nose near something in order to discover what kind of smell it has','[ transitive ]',null,'بینی خود را به چیزی نزدیک کنید تا بفهمید چه بویی دارد',array['sniff']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She bent down and smelt the flowers.","translation":"خم شد و گلها را بو کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668930.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0fee0fc3-3821-5ab4-8063-76a1a1cca0be','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',5,'have ability','توانایی دارند','spoken & written','to have the ability to notice and recognize smells','[ intransitive ]',null,'توانایی تشخیص و تشخیص بوها را داشته باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ve got a cold and I can’t smell.","translation":"من سرما خورده ام و نمی توانم بو کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000668936.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('26674e0a-3a6b-50bd-86b6-a4be4d94d0de','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'smell trouble/danger etc','بو دادن؛ استشمام کردن (بوی)؛ بو دادن (خوراک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3bc90f88-ce61-551b-a3f7-f289d2495ec0','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'smell a rat','بو دادن؛ استشمام کردن (بوی)؛ بو دادن (خوراک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ec073698-90b3-5a0d-bd7b-81f7fa817ff1','75404ecc-c6e1-51b0-ba23-ea7c59169a19',8,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'smell wrong/fishy/odd etc','بو دادن؛ استشمام کردن (بوی)؛ بو دادن (خوراک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('df6180e4-eef2-50d2-bdb4-46231d42b051','d969032a-f5fd-523f-99f3-56de43a8d61a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make your mouth curve upwards , in order to be friendly or because you are happy or amused','[ intransitive ]',null,'لبخند زدن، لبخند؛ لبخند (فرد)؛ لذت (لبخند)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['smile broadly (= very happily, with a wide smile ) He sat there smiling broadly.','smile warmly (= in a friendly way ) The man looked at Kim and smiled warmly.','smile faintly/slightly (= a little ) I saw her smile faintly at the memory.','smile politely I shook his hand and smiled politely.','smile sweetly (= in a friendly way, sometimes not sincerely ) I smiled sweetly and walked away.','smile ruefully written (= in a slightly sad way ) ‘I’m sorry, ’ she said, and smiled ruefully.','smile wryly written (= when a situation is bad but also amusing ) Carew looked at the mess and smiled wryly to himself.','smile thinly written (= a little, not in a happy or friendly way ) She smiled thinly. He would be sorry one day.','smile weakly written (= without energy or confidence ) ‘It’s OK, ’ she said, and smiled weakly.','smile grimly written (= when pleased or amused in an unpleasant situation ) The guard smiled grimly.','smile to yourself Maggie looked at the photo and smiled to herself.','make somebody smile His comment made her smile.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Susan smiled at him and waved.","translation":"سوزان به او لبخند زد و دست تکان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000669071.mp3"},{"sentence":"She had to smile at his enthusiasm (= she was amused by it ) .","translation":"او مجبور بود به شور و شوق او لبخند بزند (= او از آن سرگرم شد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585798.mp3"},{"sentence":"her smiling face","translation":"چهره خندان او","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585807.mp3"},{"sentence":"I haven’t had much to smile about lately.","translation":"من اخیراً چیز زیادی برای لبخند زدن نداشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585810.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mark read the message and smiled to himself.","translation":"مارک پیام را خواند و با خودش لبخند زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585813.mp3"},{"sentence":"They all smiled at me.","translation":"همه به من لبخند زدند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('964b078c-4b8a-5aa8-935f-0d246b3fcfa5','d969032a-f5fd-523f-99f3-56de43a8d61a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to say or express something with a smile','[ transitive ]',null,'گفتن یا بیان چیزی با لبخند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['smile broadly (= very happily, with a wide smile ) He sat there smiling broadly.','smile warmly (= in a friendly way ) The man looked at Kim and smiled warmly.','smile faintly/slightly (= a little ) I saw her smile faintly at the memory.','smile politely I shook his hand and smiled politely.','smile sweetly (= in a friendly way, sometimes not sincerely ) I smiled sweetly and walked away.','smile ruefully written (= in a slightly sad way ) ‘I’m sorry, ’ she said, and smiled ruefully.','smile wryly written (= when a situation is bad but also amusing ) Carew looked at the mess and smiled wryly to himself.','smile thinly written (= a little, not in a happy or friendly way ) She smiled thinly. He would be sorry one day.','smile weakly written (= without energy or confidence ) ‘It’s OK, ’ she said, and smiled weakly.','smile grimly written (= when pleased or amused in an unpleasant situation ) The guard smiled grimly.','smile to yourself Maggie looked at the photo and smiled to herself.','make somebody smile His comment made her smile.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘It’s good to have you back, ’ she smiled.","translation":"او لبخند زد: \"خوب است که شما برگشتید.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000669082.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('eb6229cc-37bf-5e68-af91-873cda14a2d9','d969032a-f5fd-523f-99f3-56de43a8d61a',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'fortune/the gods etc smile on somebody','لبخند زدن، لبخند؛ لبخند (فرد)؛ لذت (لبخند)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['smile broadly (= very happily, with a wide smile ) He sat there smiling broadly.','smile warmly (= in a friendly way ) The man looked at Kim and smiled warmly.','smile faintly/slightly (= a little ) I saw her smile faintly at the memory.','smile politely I shook his hand and smiled politely.','smile sweetly (= in a friendly way, sometimes not sincerely ) I smiled sweetly and walked away.','smile ruefully written (= in a slightly sad way ) ‘I’m sorry, ’ she said, and smiled ruefully.','smile wryly written (= when a situation is bad but also amusing ) Carew looked at the mess and smiled wryly to himself.','smile thinly written (= a little, not in a happy or friendly way ) She smiled thinly. He would be sorry one day.','smile weakly written (= without energy or confidence ) ‘It’s OK, ’ she said, and smiled weakly.','smile grimly written (= when pleased or amused in an unpleasant situation ) The guard smiled grimly.','smile to yourself Maggie looked at the photo and smiled to herself.','make somebody smile His comment made her smile.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1e211eb1-a626-5b5d-944d-acc24184333b','8e02b5a5-b93a-5589-9ea0-351608eebb0d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an expression in which your mouth curves upwards, when you are being friendly or are happy or amused',null,null,'لبخند، لبخند (زیبا)؛ لبخند (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give (somebody) a smile The boy gave a friendly smile.','flash (somebody) a smile (= give a quick smile ) She flashed him a smile.','have a smile on your face/lips They all had broad smiles on their faces.','be all smiles (= be happy or friendly and smile a lot ) One moment he’s all smiles, the next moment he shouts at me.','force/manage a smile (= smile when you do not really feel happy or friendly ) She forced a smile, but he could see disappointment in her face.','wear a smile (= have a smile on your face ) She wore a self-confident smile.','return somebody’s smile (= smile back at someone ) I smiled at him, but he didn’t return my smile.','somebody breaks into a smile/somebody’s face breaks into a smile (= they suddenly smile ) Anna’s face broke into a smile at the prospect of a guest.','a smile spreads across somebody’s face (= they smile ) A faint smile spread across her face.','somebody’s smile broadens (= it gets bigger ) His smile broadened when Sarah walked in.','somebody’s smile fades/vanishes (= they stop smiling ) Her smile faded and a shaft of panic shot through her.','a big/broad/wide smile (= when you are very happy ) She had a big smile on her face.','a warm/friendly smile Peter Leary welcomed Rachel with a warm smile.','a little/faint/slight smile She gave him an apologetic little smile.','a quick smile She gave him a quick smile.','a slow smile A slow smile spread across his face.','a dazzling smile (= a big smile which shows someone’s white teeth ) When he came back she gave him her most dazzling smile.','a beaming/radiant smile (= when you are very happy ) ‘I’m so pleased, ’ she told him with a beaming smile.','a bright smile written (= when you look very happy, but you may not feel happy ) She forced a bright smile.','a tight smile written (= when you are not really happy or friendly ) As he stepped past Carson he gave a quick, tight smile of acknowledgement.','a wry smile written (= when a situation is bad but also amusing ) Guy’s mouth twisted into a wry smile.','a rueful smile written (= when you feel slightly sad ) ‘I’ve been pretty stupid, haven’t I?’ Harry said with a rueful smile.','a knowing smile (= when you know something secret ) She wanted to smack him for his knowing smile.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He had a big smile on his face.","translation":"لبخند بزرگی بر لب داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001485.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Oh, I’m fine, ’ Anna replied with a smile.","translation":"آنا با لبخند پاسخ داد: اوه، من خوبم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585820.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6c308aa0-607f-5ae4-a088-2f58a841c948','f6efe744-41ca-52fc-bb20-2b73717e24d6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','white, grey , or black gas that is produced by something burning','[ uncountable ]',null,'دود، دود (سیگار)؛ دود (آتش)؛ دود (خاک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['black/blue/white/grey smoke Black smoke poured out of the engine.','thick/dense smoke Thick smoke spread through the building.','acrid smoke (= smelling bad and making you cough ) The shop was full of thick, acrid smoke.','cigarette/cigar/tobacco smoke The air was thick with cigarette smoke.','wood smoke I love the scent of wood smoke.','a cloud of smoke (= a large amount ) He lit a cigarette and blew out a cloud of smoke.','a billow of smoke (= a large amount of smoke from a fire ) The green, fresh leaves will burn slowly, with billows of smoke.','a pall of smoke (= a thick cloud of smoke hanging over something ) A thick pall of smoke hung over Cape Town.','a column/plume of smoke He could see a thin black column of smoke rising vertically into the sky.','a puff of smoke (= a small amount that comes quickly from something ) There was a puff of white smoke from the man''s gun.','a wisp of smoke (= a thin amount of smoke ) Only a few wisps of smoke rose here and there.','smoke rises Smoke was rising from the top of the tower.','smoke billows (= large amounts come from a fire ) She noticed smoke billowing out of one of the bedrooms.','smoke drifts The cigarette smoke drifted away on the breeze.','smoke curls Smoke curled from cooking fires next to a group of tents.','smoke clears (= disappears ) The kitchen door was still open, and inside the smoke was clearing.','belch (out) smoke (= send out large amounts of smoke ) The factories belch smoke.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"clouds of black smoke","translation":"ابرهای دود سیاه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000669307.mp3"},{"sentence":"cigarette smoke","translation":"دود سیگار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000669308.mp3"},{"sentence":"Smoke from burning fields drifted across nearby roads.","translation":"دود حاصل از مزارع در حال سوختن در جاده های مجاور سرازیر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585875.mp3"},{"sentence":"the pall of smoke (= thick cloud of smoke ) that hung over the city","translation":"دود (= ابر غلیظ دود) که بر شهر آویزان بود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001585876.mp3"},{"sentence":"Rangers watched from their fire towers for any wisps of smoke.","translation":"رنجرها از برج های آتش نشانی خود را برای هر گونه دود تماشا می کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001979668.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('c081dec7-1d3f-59d1-ba4f-ffcac0639cf8','f6efe744-41ca-52fc-bb20-2b73717e24d6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an act of smoking a cigarette etc','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'عمل کشیدن سیگار و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['black/blue/white/grey smoke Black smoke poured out of the engine.','thick/dense smoke Thick smoke spread through the building.','acrid smoke (= smelling bad and making you cough ) The shop was full of thick, acrid smoke.','cigarette/cigar/tobacco smoke The air was thick with cigarette smoke.','wood smoke I love the scent of wood smoke.','a cloud of smoke (= a large amount ) He lit a cigarette and blew out a cloud of smoke.','a billow of smoke (= a large amount of smoke from a fire ) The green, fresh leaves will burn slowly, with billows of smoke.','a pall of smoke (= a thick cloud of smoke hanging over something ) A thick pall of smoke hung over Cape Town.','a column/plume of smoke He could see a thin black column of smoke rising vertically into the sky.','a puff of smoke (= a small amount that comes quickly from something ) There was a puff of white smoke from the man''s gun.','a wisp of smoke (= a thin amount of smoke ) Only a few wisps of smoke rose here and there.','smoke rises Smoke was rising from the top of the tower.','smoke billows (= large amounts come from a fire ) She noticed smoke billowing out of one of the bedrooms.','smoke drifts The cigarette smoke drifted away on the breeze.','smoke curls Smoke curled from cooking fires next to a group of tents.','smoke clears (= disappears ) The kitchen door was still open, and inside the smoke was clearing.','belch (out) smoke (= send out large amounts of smoke ) The factories belch smoke.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He went outside for a quiet smoke.","translation":"او برای یک دود آرام بیرون رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000669313.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
