('4206fe8c-4455-54ab-8d7e-0f55c46f499e','68dee014-e672-52a1-b88c-c1b65d6e50dc',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to look at something or someone for a long time without moving your eyes, for example because you are surprised , angry , or bored',null,null,'خیره شدن، خیره (نگاه)؛ خیره (حس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stare hard/intently (= very steadily, with a lot of attention ) She stared hard at him for a moment.','stare fixedly (= without moving your head or eyes ) Harry stared fixedly out of the window.','stare blankly (= without emotion, understanding, or interest ) Lucy stared blankly at the teacher.','stare unseeingly/blindly literary (= not noticing anything, although your eyes are open ) She sat down on the bed and stared unseeingly at the wall.','stare vacantly (= seeming not to notice or be thinking anything ) Mum was staring vacantly at the fire.','stare moodily (= rather unhappily ) He was staring moodily into his glass.','stare in disbelief/horror/amazement etc Hilary stared in disbelief at the kitchen clock.','stare into space (= look for a long time at nothing ) Jo''s always lying on the sofa staring into space.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"What are you staring at?","translation":"به چی خیره شدی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639054.mp3"},{"sentence":"She stared at me in disbelief.","translation":"با ناباوری به من خیره شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001651927.mp3"},{"sentence":"She sat there staring into space (= looking for a long time at nothing ) .","translation":"او آنجا نشست و به فضا خیره شد (= برای مدت طولانی به دنبال هیچ چیزی نبود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001651929.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7948c645-012f-5495-81fd-be4b77b36545','68dee014-e672-52a1-b88c-c1b65d6e50dc',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be staring somebody in the face','خیره شدن، خیره (نگاه)؛ خیره (حس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['stare hard/intently (= very steadily, with a lot of attention ) She stared hard at him for a moment.','stare fixedly (= without moving your head or eyes ) Harry stared fixedly out of the window.','stare blankly (= without emotion, understanding, or interest ) Lucy stared blankly at the teacher.','stare unseeingly/blindly literary (= not noticing anything, although your eyes are open ) She sat down on the bed and stared unseeingly at the wall.','stare vacantly (= seeming not to notice or be thinking anything ) Mum was staring vacantly at the fire.','stare moodily (= rather unhappily ) He was staring moodily into his glass.','stare in disbelief/horror/amazement etc Hilary stared in disbelief at the kitchen clock.','stare into space (= look for a long time at nothing ) Jo''s always lying on the sofa staring into space.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0a5dcd2d-0717-5cb4-be75-06737a51b862','6cc64e5e-5959-5d92-a31d-27da4fcb946b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','when you look at something or someone for a long time in a steady way',null,null,'وقتی به چیزی یا شخصی برای مدت طولانی به طور ثابت نگاه می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give somebody a stare Doyle gave her a long stare.','fix somebody with a stare literary (= stare at someone ) He fixed her with a cool stare.','return somebody’s stare (= stare back at them ) I returned his stare and he looked away.','meet somebody’s stare (= look back at them ) Alan met Susan’s outraged stare calmly.','a hard stare (= very steady, with a lot of attention ) As he passed, he gave us a hard stare.','a long stare The man fixed him with a long, deliberate stare.','a blank stare (= showing no emotion, understanding, or interest ) Mention his name, and you get mostly blank stares.','a vacant stare (= seeming not to notice or be thinking anything ) She was gazing out of the window with a vacant stare.','a fixed/unwavering/unblinking stare (= with your eyes not moving at all ) His unwavering stare was making me feel pretty uneasy.','a cold/stony stare (= unfriendly ) I smiled and said "hello" but only got a cold stare.','a cool stare (= calm ) When I expressed surprise, he responded with a cool stare.','curious stares They ignored the curious stares directed at them.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She gave him a long hard stare .","translation":"نگاهی سخت و طولانی به او انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639112.mp3"},{"sentence":"She laughed, ignoring the stares of everyone around her.","translation":"او خندید، بدون توجه به نگاه های اطرافیانش.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639113.mp3"},{"sentence":"His pleas were met by a blank stare (= a stare with no expression, understanding, or interest ) .","translation":"التماس های او با یک نگاه خالی (= خیره بدون بیان، درک یا علاقه) مواجه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001651948.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('aaceacb8-ba63-5956-b495-bd3fa4b27eda','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',1,'begin doing something','شروع به انجام کاری','spoken & written','to do something that you were not doing before, and continue doing it','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'شروع کردن، آغاز کردن (کار)؛ راه‌اندازی کردن (شرکت)؛ شروع (موسیقی)',array['begin']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There’s so much to do I don’t know where to start.","translation":"کارهای زیادی برای انجام دادن وجود دارد که نمی دانم از کجا شروع کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639415.mp3"},{"sentence":"Have you started your homework?","translation":"آیا مشق شب خود را شروع کرده اید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639414.mp3"},{"sentence":"Then the baby started crying.","translation":"بعد بچه شروع کرد به گریه کردن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635554.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s starting to rain.","translation":"باران شروع به باریدن می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639411.mp3"},{"sentence":"He got up and started running again .","translation":"بلند شد و دوباره شروع به دویدن کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635557.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’d better get started (= start doing something ) soon.","translation":"بهتر است زودتر شروع کنم (= شروع به انجام کاری کنم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639437.mp3"},{"sentence":"What Kerry said started me thinking (= made me start thinking ) .","translation":"آنچه کری گفت مرا به فکر انداخت (= باعث شد شروع به فکر کردن کنم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639467.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('a5e00e7a-ee8a-58d4-b4e6-d319ce12ecaa','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',2,'begin happening','شروع به اتفاق افتادن','spoken & written','to begin happening, or to make something begin happening','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'شروع به اتفاق افتادن، یا کاری کردن که چیزی شروع شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"What time does the film start?","translation":"فیلم ساعت چند شروع می شود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639458.mp3"},{"sentence":"Lightning started a fire that burned 500 acres.","translation":"رعد و برق آتشی به راه انداخت که 500 هکتار را سوزاند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635571.mp3"},{"sentence":"The party was just getting started when Sara arrived.","translation":"مهمانی تازه شروع شده بود که سارا آمد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635572.mp3"},{"sentence":"You have two hours to complete the test, starting now.","translation":"از هم اکنون دو ساعت فرصت دارید تا آزمون را کامل کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639473.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('acc35eee-34eb-5096-b898-242a712992f9','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',3,'begin in a particular way','به روشی خاص شروع شود','spoken & written','to begin something in a particular way, or to begin in a particular way','[ intransitive always + adverb/preposition, transitive ]',null,'شروع کردن چیزی به روشی خاص یا شروع کردن به روشی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"A healthy breakfast is a good way to start the day.","translation":"یک صبحانه سالم راه خوبی برای شروع روز است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635579.mp3"},{"sentence":"The festivities started with a huge fireworks display.","translation":"این جشن با یک آتش بازی بزرگ آغاز شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635582.mp3"},{"sentence":"The restaurant started as a small take-out place.","translation":"رستوران به عنوان یک مکان کوچک برای بیرون رفتن شروع به کار کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635585.mp3"},{"sentence":"Any new exercise program should start slowly.","translation":"هر برنامه ورزشی جدید باید به آرامی شروع شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639500.mp3"},{"sentence":"Chao starts by explaining some basic legal concepts.","translation":"چائو با توضیح برخی مفاهیم اساسی حقوقی شروع می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635588.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('8e9541e0-15c7-5aea-b890-007f9279b32b','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',4,'business/organization','کسب و کار/سازمان','spoken & written','to make something begin to exist','[ transitive ]',null,'برای اینکه چیزی شروع به وجود کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She wanted to start her own catering business.","translation":"او می خواست کسب و کار خود را راه اندازی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639586.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7f3e1049-4e79-5a56-9f57-a5097ace6a67','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',5,'job/school','شغل/مدرسه','spoken & written','to begin a new job, or to begin going to school, college etc','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای شروع یک شغل جدید، یا شروع به رفتن به مدرسه، دانشگاه و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"When can you start?","translation":"چه زمانی می توانید شروع کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639514.mp3"},{"sentence":"I started college last week.","translation":"من هفته گذشته دانشگاه را شروع کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639517.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ef02dc00-3117-5f9c-aedb-0325f9a71123','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',6,'car/engine etc','ماشین / موتور و غیره','spoken & written','if you start a car or engine, or if it starts, it begins to work','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اگر ماشین یا موتوری را روشن کنید، یا اگر روشن شود، شروع به کار می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The car wouldn’t start this morning.","translation":"امروز صبح ماشین روشن نشد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639563.mp3"},{"sentence":"He couldn’t get his motorbike started.","translation":"او نتوانست موتورش را روشن کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639566.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('3e00fa0d-0915-59ab-9448-52c3f7b6795d','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',7,'begin going somewhere','شروع به رفتن به جایی','spoken & written','to begin travelling or moving in a particular direction','[ intransitive ]',null,'برای شروع سفر یا حرکت در یک جهت خاص',array['set out']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’ll have to start early to get there by lunchtime.","translation":"باید زود شروع کنیم تا تا ناهار به آنجا برسیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639527.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('307dd536-a48b-547d-84f5-edff8f7a4af8','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',8,'life/profession','زندگی / حرفه','spoken & written','to begin your life or profession in a particular way or place','[ intransitive always + adverb/preposition, transitive ]',null,'برای شروع زندگی یا حرفه خود در یک راه یا مکان خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She started as a dancer in the 1950s.","translation":"او به عنوان یک رقصنده در دهه 1950 شروع کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639541.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s difficult for new lawyers to get started in private practice.","translation":"شروع کار خصوصی برای وکلای جدید دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635589.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('612bb712-ceda-5de5-95c2-ed2ca7a4794a','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',9,'road/river/path etc','جاده / رودخانه / مسیر و غیره','spoken & written','if a river, road, path etc starts somewhere, it begins in that place','[ intransitive always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'اگر رودخانه، جاده، مسیر و غیره از جایی شروع شود، از همان مکان شروع می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The trail starts immediately behind the hotel.","translation":"مسیر بلافاصله از پشت هتل شروع می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635593.mp3"},{"sentence":"The race will start at the town hall.","translation":"مسابقه از تالار شهر آغاز خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635594.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6639b37b-e090-582b-8e38-4d5a5c98f8a1','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',10,'prices/amounts','قیمت/مقدار','spoken & written','if prices, amounts, or rates start at or from a particular number, that is the lowest number at which you can get or buy something','[ intransitive always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'اگر قیمت‌ها، مقادیر یا نرخ‌ها از یک عدد یا از یک عدد خاص شروع می‌شوند، این کمترین عددی است که می‌توانید چیزی را از آن دریافت یا خریداری کنید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Room prices start from £25 a night.","translation":"قیمت اتاق ها از شبی 25 پوند شروع می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639574.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b88ddad0-5c14-526c-8e4d-7c9344484b08','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',11,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'start from scratch/zero','شروع کردن، آغاز کردن (کار)؛ راه‌اندازی کردن (شرکت)؛ شروع (موسیقی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('068dc33d-06ee-553b-8315-f16e231b6b8f','617cf9b9-abbc-5101-9dbf-16001d326989',12,'deliberately begin something','عمداً چیزی را شروع کنم','spoken & written','to deliberately make something start happening, especially something bad','[ transitive ]',null,'عمدا کاری کردن که اتفاقی بیفتد، به خصوص اتفاق بد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I started a fire to warm the place up.","translation":"آتش زدم تا محل را گرم کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635603.mp3"},{"sentence":"Oh, don’t go trying to start an argument.","translation":"اوه، سعی نکنید بحثی را شروع کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635609.mp3"},{"sentence":"Other girls were starting rumours about me.","translation":"دختران دیگر در مورد من شایعات را شروع کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635610.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
