('98ae5231-654a-5e31-92b3-0002b50506df','aa6c718d-4aec-5ebb-84ac-499b5f7a0200',1,'of an activity/event','از یک فعالیت/رویداد','spoken & written','the first part of an activity or event, or the point at which it begins to develop','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'شروع، آغاز (کار)؛ استارت (ماشین)؛ شروع (مسابقه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a good/great start A 3-0 win is a good start for the team.','a flying start (= a very good start ) The appeal got off to a flying start at the weekend when the group held a raffle.','a promising start (= a good start that makes success seem likely ) Her teacher says she''s made a promising start in learning Spanish.','a bad/poor/disastrous start Things got off to a bad start when two people turned up late.','a rocky/shaky start (= a rather bad start ) After a shaky start, they managed two wins in five matches.','a disappointing start He accepted full responsibility for the club’s disappointing start to the season.','a slow start Work got off to a very slow start because of bad weather.','an auspicious/inauspicious start (= one that makes it seem likely that something will be good or bad ) His second term in office has got off to an extremely inauspicious start.','an early/late start It was long trip so we had planned an early start.','get off to a good/bad etc start On your first day at work, you want to get off to a good start.','make a good/bad/early etc start He made a flying start at college, but then he didn''t manage to keep it up.','have a good/bad etc start We’ve had a disappointing start but we are hoping to improve.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We arrived late and missed the start of the film.","translation":"دیر رسیدیم و شروع فیلم را از دست دادیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639741.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ve had problems with this project right from the start.","translation":"ما از همان ابتدا با این پروژه مشکل داشتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639744.mp3"},{"sentence":"She read the letter from start to finish without looking up.","translation":"او نامه را از ابتدا تا انتها خواند بدون اینکه سرش را بلند کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639747.mp3"},{"sentence":"a free bottle of wine to get your holiday off to a great start","translation":"یک بطری شراب رایگان برای شروع عالی برای تعطیلات خود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001983101.mp3"},{"sentence":"After a rocky start, the show is now very popular.","translation":"پس از یک شروع دشوار، این نمایش اکنون بسیار محبوب شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635727.mp3"},{"sentence":"He wanted an early start on his election campaign.","translation":"او خواستار شروع زودهنگام مبارزات انتخاباتی خود بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635728.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('73685d7e-eaf8-5d64-a4ea-84938adccd28','aa6c718d-4aec-5ebb-84ac-499b5f7a0200',2,'of a period of time','یک دوره زمانی','spoken & written','the first part of a particular period of time','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'بخش اول یک دوره زمانی خاص',array['beginning']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a good/great start A 3-0 win is a good start for the team.','a flying start (= a very good start ) The appeal got off to a flying start at the weekend when the group held a raffle.','a promising start (= a good start that makes success seem likely ) Her teacher says she''s made a promising start in learning Spanish.','a bad/poor/disastrous start Things got off to a bad start when two people turned up late.','a rocky/shaky start (= a rather bad start ) After a shaky start, they managed two wins in five matches.','a disappointing start He accepted full responsibility for the club’s disappointing start to the season.','a slow start Work got off to a very slow start because of bad weather.','an auspicious/inauspicious start (= one that makes it seem likely that something will be good or bad ) His second term in office has got off to an extremely inauspicious start.','an early/late start It was long trip so we had planned an early start.','get off to a good/bad etc start On your first day at work, you want to get off to a good start.','make a good/bad/early etc start He made a flying start at college, but then he didn''t manage to keep it up.','have a good/bad etc start We’ve had a disappointing start but we are hoping to improve.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Since the start of 1992, the company has doubled in size.","translation":"از آغاز سال 1992، اندازه شرکت دو برابر شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001635734.mp3"},{"sentence":"the start of an election year","translation":"آغاز سال انتخابات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000639759.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
